From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Yi Xie <imxieyi@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 11:19:12 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] gallivm: convert a NaN to the lower bound without SSE2

lp_build_conv converts floats to unsigned normalized bytes with SSE2
or AltiVec packs, which turn a NaN into 0. Every other CPU, arm64
included, takes the generic path. Its lower clamp kept a NaN, because
lp_build_max compares unordered, and the conversion after it adds a
bias and reads the result out of the low mantissa bits, so a NaN
became the low byte of its own payload.

A fragment shader that wrote a NaN to an RGBA8 target on arm64 stored
that byte. dEQP-GLES31.functional.copy_image.mixed fills an RGBA32F
image with ASTC void-extent blocks, whose first two words are NaNs,
renders it and expects 0 there, so llvmpipe failed every ASTC and
RGBA32F pair.

The lower clamp now returns its bound for a NaN, as the SSE2 path and
the x86 max instruction already do.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/gallium/auxiliary/gallivm/lp_bld_conv.c | 8 +++++++-
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/gallium/auxiliary/gallivm/lp_bld_conv.c b/src/gallium/auxiliary/gallivm/lp_bld_conv.c
index ac1d442b1e92ed0ca422a86e0f61607193ba2547..f21d9334cfa75f269b8eb83b254422512f842940 100644
--- a/src/gallium/auxiliary/gallivm/lp_bld_conv.c
+++ b/src/gallium/auxiliary/gallivm/lp_bld_conv.c
@@ -833,8 +833,14 @@ lp_build_conv(struct gallivm_state *gallivm,
             thres = bld.zero;
          else
             thres = lp_build_const_vec(gallivm, src_type, dst_min);
+         /*
+          * A NaN becomes the lower bound, as in the SSE2 fast path above.
+          * Otherwise it reaches the conversion below, which reads an
+          * unsigned normalized result out of the low mantissa bits.
+          */
          for(i = 0; i < num_tmps; ++i)
-            tmp[i] = lp_build_max(&bld, tmp[i], thres);
+            tmp[i] = lp_build_max_ext(&bld, tmp[i], thres,
+                                      GALLIVM_NAN_RETURN_OTHER_SECOND_NONNAN);
       }
 
       if(src_max > dst_max) {
